                <pb facs="0768" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4 A 2/273: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-12T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 12,
                                1925—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Your No. 9, February 9, 4 p.m. Referring to Department’s No. 4, February 7, 3
                    p.m., you may substitute “with respect to” for “toward suppressing illicit” in
                    note to Persian Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
